<%# 
====================================================================
FILE: src/views/register.ejs
COURSE: CSE 340 - Web Backend Development (Week 5)
====================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH: The sign-up page where a new person creates an account.
LOGIC: Shown by showUserRegistrationForm (GET /register). When submitted,
       the form sends name, email, and password to POST /register.
WHY WE NEED IT: People need a form to type their info before an account exists.
LEARNING GAP: The data typed here goes to req.body in src/controllers/users.js.
              The password travels to the server as typed; the server hashes it
              before saving. The database never stores the real password.
%>
<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main>
    <%# title comes from the controller: res.render('register', { title: 'Register' }) %>
    <h1><%= title %></h1>

    <%# 
    PLAIN ENGLISH: The form itself.
    LOGIC: method="POST" sends the data privately in the request body.
           action="/register" sends it to the POST /register route.
    WHY WE NEED IT: Connects this form to processUserRegistrationForm.
    LEARNING GAP: GET would put the password in the web address, where anyone
                  could see it. POST keeps it out of the address bar.
    %>
    <form action="/register" method="POST">

        <%# 
        PLAIN ENGLISH: Name box.
        LOGIC: name="name" becomes req.body.name in the controller.
        WHY WE NEED IT: Stores the person's display name in users.name.
        LEARNING GAP: The label's for="name" matches the input's id="name",
                      so clicking the label jumps into the box (helps accessibility).
        %>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="name">Name</label>
            <input
                type="text"
                id="name"
                name="name"
                required
            />
        </div>
        
        <%# 
        PLAIN ENGLISH: Email box (this is the username).
        LOGIC: type="email" makes the browser check for a real email format.
        WHY WE NEED IT: Email is how the person will log in, and it must be unique.
        LEARNING GAP: The browser check is for convenience only. The real safety
                      check is on the server (the UNIQUE rule in the database).
        %>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="email">Email (Username)</label>
            <input
                type="email"
                id="email"
                name="email"
                required
            />
        </div>

        <%# 
        PLAIN ENGLISH: Password box.
        LOGIC: type="password" shows dots instead of the letters typed.
        WHY WE NEED IT: The controller hashes this with bcrypt before saving.
        LEARNING GAP: Hiding the letters on screen is not the same as security.
                      Hashing on the server is what actually protects it.
        %>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="password">Password</label>
            <input
                type="password"
                id="password"
                name="password"
                required
            />
        </div>

        <button type="submit">Register</button>
    </form>

</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
